module gunbc.fleet_acoustic_intent

import std.types { Bool, NonEmptyStr }
import std.measure { Percent, percent }
import std.dissolution { DissolutionCondition, unbound_dissolution }
import product.acoustic_ceiling {
  AcousticCeilingBasis,
  OperatorStatedTolerance,
}
import product.fan_policy_standing {
  FanDutyCeilingVerdict,
  FanPolicyStanding,
  fan_policy_against_duty_ceiling,
}

// THE SITE'S ACOUSTIC INTENT, WHICH IS A POLICY THE OPERATOR STATES AND NOT A NUMBER ANYTHING READ.
//
// The machines under test sit in the operator's own residence, and on 2026-09-18 he stated the
// constraint in behavioural terms: he cannot tolerate fans running at sustained full duty while he
// is testing. That sentence is the whole input, and what follows is an exercise in NOT making it
// into more than it is.
//
// WHAT IT IS: a bound on DUTY. It is enforceable today, against any controller that reports duty,
// with no instrument and no datasheet in between.
//
// WHAT IT IS NOT: a dB(A) figure. No sound level was measured at any position and the operator
// stated none, so this module declares no acoustic ceiling row. That absence is deliberate and it is
// the §4d discipline applied to the easiest possible place to violate it - a plausible number here
// (45 dB(A) at one metre, say) would read as the operator's constraint forever, and the person it
// misrepresents is the one who has to live with the result.
//
// THE SITE IS THE ONE ALREADY DECLARED. gunbc.fleet_physical_inventory operator_site is where these
// machines are; minting a second identity for the same place - "operator-residence" beside
// "operator-lab" - would be the §3 fork, arrived at from the direction where both spellings look
// reasonable.
//
// AND AN ALIAS ROW IS THAT FORK, which this module argued against and then committed anyway. It
// carried `data operator_residence_site: SiteIdentity = operator_site` directly beneath the
// paragraph above - a second name for one concept, with no consumer at all, so it was §3 nicknaming
// and §3c dangling at once. Deleted rather than wired up: a caller that needs this site imports
// operator_site, which is the name that already exists.
// THE DUTY THE OPERATOR WILL TOLERATE SUSTAINED, AS A CEILING AND NOT A TARGET.
//
// Sixty percent is the operator's stated boundary read conservatively: "not sustained full duty" is
// what he said, and a ceiling at 99 would satisfy the letter of it while being, in a residence,
// exactly the thing he was objecting to. This number is OPERATOR POLICY and carries no measurement
// behind it, which is why it sits beside the basis row below rather than alone - a bare percent
// would be indistinguishable from a datasheet figure to anybody reading it later.
//
// IT SEPARATES THE SUSTAINED STATE FROM THE EXCURSION RATHER THAN EXEMPTING THE EXCURSION, and the
// difference between those two sentences is a defect this module's prose once carried. An earlier
// revision claimed the ceiling did not apply to a pre-POST failsafe "which is why the consuming
// function takes a standing rather than a bare reading" - while that function projected the drive
// out of the standing and compared it, so a pre-POST failsafe at 100% came back plain over-ceiling.
// The prose promised a discrimination the fold did not make (DESIGN §4c: an annotation is never
// evidence that a machine claim holds).
//
// The fold now branches, and what it branches to is NOT an exemption: a controller with no host
// thermals has no safe alternative to a high fixed output, so its excursion cannot be converged
// away by lowering a curve - it is bounded by DURATION and, in the last resort, by the operator
// powering the machine off. That is exactly what he described on Mt. Jade, where the excursion was
// unbounded because the host never posted. So a failsafe over this ceiling is still OVER it; it is
// reported as FanDutyExcursionOverCeiling carrying its window, and only a steady curve over the
// ceiling is a converge obligation.
data operator_residence_sustained_duty_ceiling: Percent = percent(60)

data operator_residence_duty_ceiling_basis: AcousticCeilingBasis = OperatorStatedTolerance { statement: "operator statement 2026-09-18: cannot tolerate sustained full-duty fans in the residence during testing; the percentage is this repository's conservative reading of that sentence and not a figure the operator gave" }

// THE ENFORCEABLE CONSUMER, TODAY. This is what the fan-policy lane actually calls: a standing
// observed at a host in this residence, bounded by the duty the operator will tolerate. Every arm of
// the verdict is reachable - within, over, and the tach-only refusal, which is the arm Mt. Collins
// itself lands on while its controller reports fans in RPM.
fn residence_duty_verdict(standing: FanPolicyStanding) -> FanDutyCeilingVerdict {
  fan_policy_against_duty_ceiling(standing: standing, ceiling: operator_residence_sustained_duty_ceiling)
}

// THE ACOUSTIC ROUTE IS A DECLARED FRONTIER, NOT A DANGLING DECLARATION (DESIGN §3c).
//
// A SIGNATURE-IDENTICAL WRAPPER STOOD HERE AND WAS THE SAME NICKNAME THIS MODULE DELETED FOUR
// PARAGRAPHS ABOVE, in function form rather than row form: residence_duty_ceiling_from_datasheet
// bound no ceiling, no row and no count, forwarded every argument unchanged, and existed only to
// give the frontier row something local to name. The frontier names duty_ceiling_for_fan directly
// now, which is the declaration that actually does the work.
//
// TWO FOLDS WAIT ON THE SAME MISSING FACT: product.acoustic_ceiling duty_ceiling_for_fan, which
// derives a duty bound from a fan's published table under a stated dB(A) ceiling, and
// product.fan_policy_standing fan_policy_against_ceiling, which bounds a standing by that ceiling
// and carries the typed refusal for a family whose converge route is unbound. Both are executed by
// witnesses - against a catalogued fan, a real standing, and both family routes, the OpenBMC one
// citing extdeps.bmc.openbmc_fan_control declarations that resolve - and neither has a production
// consumer, because this site has no dB(A) ceiling to state. They share one trigger because they
// wait on one fact.
//
// TRIGGER, stated as the CAPABILITY and not as an artifact: a stated-or-measured dB(A) ceiling for
// this site at a named reference position, TOGETHER WITH a modeled fan part for the host being
// bounded. Both are required and neither alone retires this row - a ceiling with no catalogued fan
// has nothing to compare against, and a catalogued fan with no ceiling has no bound. Mt. Jade's six
// 6056 fans landing from the platform lane satisfies the second half only.
data residence_acoustic_ceiling_frontier: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(description: "dissolves when this site carries a stated-or-measured dB(A) ceiling at a named reference position AND the host being bounded has a modeled fan part, at which point product.acoustic_ceiling duty_ceiling_for_fan and product.fan_policy_standing fan_policy_against_ceiling both gain production consumers; a catalogued fan without a ceiling, or a ceiling without a catalogued fan, retires neither half")
